      "source": "main p3 Table1 and Fig1a; SI p22",
      "classification": "public experiment, calculated transitions private"
    },
    {
      "element": "scope boundary",
      "source": "main pp3–4 separate molecular and aggregation discussions",
      "classification": "finite solution subproblem"
    }
  ],
  "public_facts_and_constraints": "The source compound2a is C18H20B10, a neutral singlet with a12-vertex closo cage and the supplied arene-fusion connectivity. Cage adjacency encodes a multicenter cluster topology, not an assertion that every cage edge is an ordinary localized two-center bond. Use the same molecule under THF solution conditions; the source measured absorption and emission quantities are public facts. Molecular conformations and excited states are to be investigated, not supplied as answers.",
  "agent_decisions": [
    "Choose a molecular/excited-state description capable of accounting for the source solution spectra.",
    "Develop explanations and informative calculations/comparisons within the same chemical system.",
    "Determine which state or structural assignments are identifiable and qualify model-dependent results."
  ],
